 anatomist"},"born":129,"died":216,"approx":true,"lat":41.89,"lng":12.49,"place":{"en":"Rome"},"region":"europe","category":"science","tier":2,"bio":{"en":"Physician to Roman emperors whose anatomical and medical writings remained the authority in Europe and the Islamic world until the 16th century."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Galenus.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galen"}},{"id":"nagarjuna","name":{"en":"Nagarjuna"},"role":{"en":"Indian Buddhist philosopher"},"born":150,"died":250,"approx":true,"lat":16.52,"lng":79.24,"place":{"en":"Nagarjunakonda"},"region":"asia","category":"culture","tier":2,"bio":{"en":"Founder of Madhyamaka, the \"middle way\": things have no fixed essence of their own and exist only in dependence on one another, which is what emptiness (shunyata) means."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Nagarjuna%20at%20Samye%20Ling%20Monastery.JPG?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nagarjuna"},"schools":["madhyamaka"]},{"id":"cao-cao","name":{"en":"Cao Cao"},"role":{"en":"warlord of the Three Kingdoms era"},"born":155,"died":220,"approx":false,"lat":34.04,"lng":113.85,"place":{"en":"Xuchang"},"region":"asia","category":"war","tier":3,"bio":{"en":"Warlord and poet who unified northern China at the end of the Han dynasty; his son founded the state of Wei."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Cao%20Cao%20scth.jpg?width=160","wikipedia":{"en":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cao_Cao"}},{"id":"zhuge-liang","name":{"en":"Zhuge Liang"},"role":{"en":"chancellor of Shu Han"},"born":181,"died":234,"approx":false,"lat":30.66,"lng":104.07,"place":{"en":"Chengdu"},"region":"asia","category":"politics","tier":3,"bio":{"en":"Chancellor and strategist of Shu Han, celebrated through the Romance of the Three Kingdoms as the epitome of wisdom."},"portrait":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%E8%9C%80%E6%B1%